  "protocol": "Three fresh Chrome processes per backend and model; paired forward/reverse backend order with a rotating starting backend. Full original PLY/SH3 inputs, matched cameras and resolution, rendering settings adjusted as closely as possible, radial sorting in all depth-sorted groups and native caching. Every backend measures static and moving (±45°, 8 s real-time orbit) main and closer side views; PlayCanvas WebGPU and both GSL backends add raw stochastic rendering without spatial resolve or temporal accumulation. Frames are sampled with the lab sampler and one GPU frame in flight: each frame is submitted after the previous frame completes on the GPU; samples are intervals between submissions, FPS = frames / sampled time, with P50/P95 frame intervals. Sort latency uses a separate diagnostic with explicit completion. Memory records post-GC main and live Worker V8 heaps, external backing and WASM capacity.",
